  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing the Capacity of Ghana to Address Climate Impact on &quot;Forts and Castles of Ghana in Greater Accra Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen Ghanas capacity to address climate change impacts on its Forts and Castles, UNESCO World Heritage Site of Ghana. 
     It focuses on 1) developing a climate vulnerability database by collecting scientific data, such as 3D scans and erosion assessments, providing a solid foundation for climate impact analysis.  The project also supports the 2) establishment of national climate adaptation policies, complemented by a climate risk map that integrates cultural heritage protection into national strategies. Additionally, it emphasizes 3)capacity-building through training for site managers and policymakers, ensuring the institutionalization of knowledge and skills vital for long-term heritage preservation. This comprehensive approach not only safeguards Ghanas historical sites but also aligns cultural heritage management with broader climate resilience efforts, fostering sustainable heritage conservation practices.</narrative>
  </description>
